Derive API client functions from route definitions using VTA.
Generated fields use ordinary function application. Path parameters are
plain records; optional query parameters are explicit `Maybe` fields.

```purescript
type UserAPI = { getUser :: Route ... }
api = client @UserAPI "https://api.example.com"
user <- api.getUser { id: 42 }
users <- api.listUsers { limit: Just 10, offset: Nothing }
health <- api.health
```

Attach query parameters to a path

Example:
  Path ("users" / "id" : Int) :? { limit :: Int, offset :: Required Int }

Plain text request/response body (text/plain)

Example:
  { body :: PlainText }

JSON-encoded request body (application/json)

Example:
  Request { body :: JSON User }

Form data encoded request body (application/x-www-form-urlencoded)

Example:
  Request { body :: FormData { username :: String, password :: String } }
